logerr: line-buffer the log file with setvbuf(), not setlinebuf().

setlinebuf() is a BSD function QNX's <stdio.h> does not declare (the C
library exports it, so the implicit declaration linked). setvbuf() with
_IOLBF is the standard spelling of the same thing.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/logerr.c
+++ b/src/logerr.c
@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@
 #ifndef SMALL
 	if ((ctx->log_file = fopen(path, "ae")) == NULL)
 		return -1;
-	setlinebuf(ctx->log_file);
+	setvbuf(ctx->log_file, NULL, _IOLBF, 0);
 	return fileno(ctx->log_file);
 #else
 	errno = ENOTSUP;
